selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#pip-installer\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Pip Installer<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#pip-installer\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><h3>What is Pip?<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#what-is-pip\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>Pip is the package installer for Python. Python-based MCP servers are distributed through PyPI (Python Package Index).</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#docker-installer\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Docker Installer<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#docker-installer\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><h3>What is Docker Installation?<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#what-is-docker-installation\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>Docker allows MCP servers to run in isolated containers with all dependencies included.</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#automatic-installation-in-action\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Automatic Installation in Action<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#automatic-installation-in-action\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Expected Output:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#troubleshooting-installation-issues\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Troubleshooting Installation Issues<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#troubleshooting-installation-issues\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>When automatic installation fails, you can debug specific installer types:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#choosing-the-right-installer\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Choosing the Right Installer<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#choosing-the-right-installer\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><h3>Use NPM when:<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#use-npm-when\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#getting-started-with-haive-mcp\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Getting Started with Haive MCP<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#getting-started-with-haive-mcp\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>With Haive MCP, the process is dramatically simplified through <strong>automatic discovery</strong>:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#common-use-cases\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Common Use Cases<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#common-use-cases\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#npm-installer-most-common\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">NPM Installer (Most Common)<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#npm-installer-most-common\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><h3>What is NPM?<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#what-is-npm\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>NPM (Node Package Manager) is the package manager for JavaScript and Node.js. Many MCP servers are distributed as npm packages.</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#core-concepts\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Core Concepts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#core-concepts\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><h3>1. <strong>MCP Servers</strong><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#mcp-servers\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>MCP servers are standalone programs that expose functionality to AI models. They can:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#summary\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Summary<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#summary\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>You\u2019ve learned how to:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#how-mcp-works\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">How MCP Works<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#how-mcp-works\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#additional-resources\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Additional Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#additional-resources\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#best-practices\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Best Practices<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#best-practices\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#how-different-installation-types-work\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">How Different Installation Types Work<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#how-different-installation-types-work\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The agent automatically determines the best installation method for each server:</p>", "a[href=\"#tutorials\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Tutorials<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tutorials\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Welcome to the haive-mcp tutorials! These hands-on guides will walk you through using the Model Context Protocol (MCP) with Haive\u2019s 1900+ available servers.</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#next-steps\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Next Steps<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#next-steps\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#step-2-using-your-agent-with-file-operations\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Step 2: Using Your Agent with File Operations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#step-2-using-your-agent-with-file-operations\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Now let\u2019s use the agent to perform file operations:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#key-takeaways\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Key Takeaways<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#key-takeaways\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Tutorial 3: Automatic Installation Behind the Scenes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tutorial-3-automatic-installation-behind-the-scenes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#overview\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>While EnhancedMCPAgent handles all installation automatically, understanding how different MCP servers are installed helps you troubleshoot issues and optimize performance. Haive MCP supports <strong>all major installation methods</strong> transparently.</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#mcp-vs-traditional-apis\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">MCP vs Traditional APIs<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#mcp-vs-traditional-apis\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"guides.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Guides<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#guides\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>In-depth guides for working with haive-mcp and its 1900+ available MCP servers.</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#example-filesystem-server\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Example: Filesystem Server<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#example-filesystem-server\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The filesystem MCP server provides tools for file operations:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#key-benefits\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Key Benefits<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#key-benefits\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#next-steps\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Next Steps<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#next-steps\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#git-installer\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Git Installer<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#git-installer\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><h3>What is Git Installation?<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#what-is-git-installation\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>Some MCP servers are distributed as Git repositories that need to be cloned and set up manually.</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#overview\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#overview\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>While EnhancedMCPAgent handles all installation automatically, understanding how different MCP servers are installed helps you troubleshoot issues and optimize performance. Haive MCP supports <strong>all major installation methods</strong> transparently.</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#step-3-exploring-different-server-categories\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Step 3: Exploring Different Server Categories<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#step-3-exploring-different-server-categories\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>MCP servers are organized into categories for easy discovery:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#summary\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Summary<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#summary\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><strong>With EnhancedMCPAgent, you don\u2019t need to worry about installer types!</strong> The agent:</p>", "a[href=\"#tutorial-overview\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Tutorial Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tutorial-overview\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#step-5-common-issues-and-solutions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Step 5: Common Issues and Solutions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#step-5-common-issues-and-solutions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><h3>Issue 1: No Servers Connected<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#issue-1-no-servers-connected\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#comparison-table\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Comparison Table<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#comparison-table\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#step-1-create-your-first-mcp-enhanced-agent\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Step 1: Create Your First MCP-Enhanced Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#step-1-create-your-first-mcp-enhanced-agent\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Skip all the manual server installation! With Haive MCP, agents automatically discover and install the tools they need:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#what-is-mcp\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">What is MCP?<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#what-is-mcp\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is a standardized protocol that allows AI models to interact with external tools, resources, and data sources. With <strong>Haive MCP</strong>, agents can <strong>automatically discover and integrate</strong> tools from <strong>1900+ MCP servers</strong> at runtime, without any manual configuration.</p>", "a[href=\"#next-steps\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Next Steps<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#next-steps\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>After completing the tutorials:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Tutorial 1: Understanding MCP with Haive\u2019s Dynamic Discovery<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tutorial-1-understanding-mcp-with-haives-dynamic-discovery\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>What is MCP?<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#what-is-mcp\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is a standardized protocol that allows AI models to interact with external tools, resources, and data sources. With <strong>Haive MCP</strong>, agents can <strong>automatically discover and integrate</strong> tools from <strong>1900+ MCP servers</strong> at runtime, without any manual configuration.</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#practice-exercises\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Practice Exercises<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#practice-exercises\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#quick-start\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Quick Start<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#quick-start\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Jump right in with a simple example:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/01_understanding_mcp.html#resources\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#resources\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#prerequisites\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Prerequisites<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#prerequisites\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Before starting, ensure you have:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#available-categories\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Available Categories<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#available-categories\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"examples.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Examples<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#examples\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Comprehensive examples demonstrating haive-mcp capabilities with 1900+ MCP servers.</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Tutorial 2: Your First MCP-Enhanced Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tutorial-2-your-first-mcp-enhanced-agent\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>Prerequisites<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#prerequisites\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Before starting, ensure you have:</p>", "a[href=\"tutorials/03_installer_types.html#next-steps\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Next Steps<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#next-steps\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"tutorials/02_first_mcp_server.html#step-4-debugging-and-monitoring\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Step 4: Debugging and Monitoring<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#step-4-debugging-and-monitoring\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Monitor your MCP integration with built-in debugging tools:</p>"}
